---
import "../styles/index.css";
import { url } from "../lib/url";
---

<html>
    <head>
        <title>The Bounty Hunter Challenge — Dead by Daylight</title>
        <meta charset="UTF-8" />
        <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    </head>
    <body>
        <nav>
            <div class="wrap">
                <a class="brand" href={url("#top")}
                    >Bounty<span>Hunter</span>.challenge</a
                >
                <ul class="nav-links">
                    <li><a href={url("#goal")}>Goal</a></li>
                    <li><a href={url("#rules")}>Rules</a></li>
                    <li><a href={url("#shop")}>Shop</a></li>
                    <li><a href={url("#ladder")}>Ladder</a></li>
                    <li><a href={url("#live")}>Live</a></li>
                    <li><a href={url("/hunt")}>The Hunt</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </nav>

        <header class="hero" id="top">
            <div class="fog-layer"></div>
            <div class="wrap">
                <p class="eyebrow">
                    A self-made Dead by Daylight challenge run
                </p>
                <div class="poster">
                    <div class="stamp">Active<br />Bounty</div>
                    <h1>Wanted:<br />every survivor, <em>dead</em> once.</h1>
                    <p class="lede">
                        One killer. Zero perks. Zero add-ons. The Bounty Hunter
                        Challenge starts you at rock bottom and only lets you
                        climb by putting survivors on the hook — every single
                        one of them, at least once.
                    </p>
                    <p class="byline">
                        Devised &amp; played by <a
                            href="https://www.youtube.com/@AlexRussoYT"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener">Alex Russo</a
                        >
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="hero-cta">
                    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#rules">Read the rules</a>
                    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#video"
                        >Watch the pitch video</a
                    >
                </div>
            </div>
        </header>

        <section id="video">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Case file, on tape</p>
                    <h2>Hear it from the hunter</h2>
                    <p>
                        Alex breaks down the full challenge — why it exists, how
                        the bounty system works, and what happens the first time
                        it goes sideways.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="video-frame">
                    <iframe
                        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/r4qWOwr0h0g"
                        title="Bounty Hunter Challenge — explainer video"
                        loading="lazy"
                        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"
                        allowfullscreen></iframe>
                </div>
                <p class="video-caption">
                    Prefer YouTube directly? <a
                        href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r4qWOwr0h0g"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener">Open the video →</a
                    >
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="goal">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">The main goal</p>
                    <h2>Collect every bounty</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="goal-card">
                    <span class="goal-mark">✕</span>
                    <p>
                        The challenge is won the moment <strong
                            >every survivor in Dead by Daylight has been
                            sacrificed at least once</strong
                        >. That's the finish line, not a ceiling — survivors can be
                        hunted down again and again over the course of the run, and
                        every repeat kill still pays out. It doesn't matter how
                        strong the killer gets along the way; the run only ends
                        when the last name on the list is crossed off.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="rules">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Starting conditions</p>
                    <h2>You begin with nothing</h2>
                    <p>
                        No perks. No add-ons. No advantage. Just the weakest
                        killer in the roster and whatever you can earn from
                        here.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="start-grid">
                    <div class="stat-card" data-corner="RANK 0">
                        <h3>Killer</h3>
                        <p>
                            The weakest killer available — think Trapper or
                            Ghost Face, run completely bare. No offering, no map
                            pressure, nothing borrowed.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="stat-card" data-corner="EMPTY">
                        <h3>Loadout</h3>
                        <p>
                            Four perk slots, zero perks equipped. Every add-on
                            slot sits open until it's earned back through the
                            shop.
                        </p>
                        <div class="slot-row">
                            <div class="slot">—</div><div class="slot">
                                —
                            </div><div class="slot">—</div><div class="slot">
                                —
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Earning bounty points</p>
                    <h2>Every kill pays out, every time</h2>
                    <p>
                        Survivors aren't retired after their first kill — track
                        the same target down as many times as you can catch
                        them, and each kill awards Bounty Points based on their
                        rarity tier. Points are the only currency in this run —
                        there's no other way to gear up.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="table-wrap">
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr
                                ><th>Rarity tier</th><th>Example survivor</th
                                ><th>Bounty payout</th></tr
                            >
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr
                                ><td>Common</td><td
                                    >Kate Denson, Dwight Fairfield, Sable Ward</td
                                ><td class="pts">+1 pt</td></tr
                            >
                            <tr
                                ><td>Uncommon</td><td
                                    >Jill Valentine, Ada Wong, Yui Kimura</td
                                ><td class="pts">+2 pts</td></tr
                            >
                            <tr
                                ><td>Rare</td><td
                                    >William Bill Overbeck, Rick Grimes, Taurie
                                    Cain</td
                                ><td class="pts">+3 pts</td></tr
                            >
                            <tr
                                ><td>Very rare</td><td
                                    >Alan Wake, Felix Richter, Nicolas Cage</td
                                ><td class="pts">+5 pts</td></tr
                            >
                            <tr
                                ><td>Exotic</td><td
                                    >Laurie Strode, The Troupe, Ellen Ripley</td
                                ><td class="pts">+6 pts</td></tr
                            >
                            <tr
                                ><td>Ultra Rare</td><td
                                    >Michonne Grimes, Elodie Rakoto, Haddie Kaur</td
                                ><td class="pts">+10 pts</td></tr
                            >
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
                <p class="table-note">
                    Exact tier assignments and values are Alex's call to tune
                    per season — the table above is the shape of the system, not
                    a locked ruling.
                </p>
                <div class="bonus-note">
                    <strong>Cosmetic bonus:</strong> if the survivor is wearing a
                    skin that renames the character — Alan Wake dressed as Saga Anderson,
                    Jill Valentine as Sheva — that kill pays an extra <strong
                        >+2 bonus points</strong
                    >, no matter the base tier.
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="shop">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Spending the bounty</p>
                    <h2>The Bounty Shop</h2>
                    <p>
                        Points accumulated across matches get spent between
                        games. This is the only place gear enters the run.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="shop-grid">
                    <div class="shop-card">
                        <div class="icon">✦</div>
                        <h3>Random perks</h3>
                        <p>
                            Spend points on a perk pull from a given tier. Tiers
                            follow Otzdarva's community rankings — cheap pulls
                            land in the F/D range, and it gets pricier climbing
                            toward A and S tier.
                        </p>
                        <div class="tier-tags">
                            <span class="tier-tag">F-tier</span><span
                                class="tier-tag">D-tier</span
                            ><span class="tier-tag">C-tier</span><span
                                class="tier-tag">B-tier</span
                            ><span class="tier-tag">A-tier</span><span
                                class="tier-tag">S-tier</span
                            >
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="shop-card">
                        <div class="icon">⚒</div>
                        <h3>Add-on upgrades</h3>
                        <p>
                            Unlock add-on slots permanently, and raise their
                            rarity ceiling — brown, then green, and up — across
                            every killer in the roster, not just the one
                            currently in play.
                        </p>
                        <div class="tier-tags">
                            <span class="tier-tag">Brown</span><span
                                class="tier-tag">Yellow</span
                            ><span class="tier-tag">Green</span><span
                                class="tier-tag">Purple</span
                            ><span class="tier-tag">Pink/Iri</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="ladder">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Upgrading killers</p>
                    <h2>Climbing off the bottom rung</h2>
                    <p>
                        There are two ways to trade up to a stronger killer —
                        one is earned, one is bought.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <ol class="ladder">
                    <li>
                        <div>
                            <h3>Free upgrade — win the streak</h3>
                            <p>
                                Two matches in a row closed out with a 3-kill or
                                4-kill result promotes the current killer to the
                                next one up, no points spent.
                            </p>
                            <div class="path-tags">
                                <span class="path-tag free">free</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <div>
                            <h3>Paid upgrade — buy your way out</h3>
                            <p>
                                Stuck on a weak killer with bad matchups? Spend
                                accumulated Bounty Points to buy the next killer
                                tier outright and skip the streak requirement.
                            </p>
                            <div class="path-tags">
                                <span class="path-tag paid">paid</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </li>
                </ol>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section id="live">
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Follow the hunt</p>
                    <h2>Watch it unfold</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="live-grid">
                    <a
                        class="live-card"
                        href="https://www.twitch.tv/aleexrusso"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                    >
                        <div class="platform">
                            <span class="dot live"></span>Twitch
                        </div>
                        <h3>aleexrusso</h3>
                        <p>
                            Live runs, close calls, and the moments a bounty
                            almost slips away. Drop in while the challenge is
                            being played.
                        </p>
                    </a>
                    <a
                        class="live-card"
                        href="https://www.youtube.com/@AlexRussoYT"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener"
                    >
                        <div class="platform">
                            <span class="dot"></span>YouTube
                        </div>
                        <h3>@AlexRussoYT</h3>
                        <p>
                            VODs, highlights, and the full breakdown videos for
                            the challenge and whatever comes after it.
                        </p>
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section>
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="section-head">
                    <p class="section-tag">Behind the site</p>
                    <h2>Tech loadout</h2>
                </div>
                <div class="tech-card">
                    <div class="tech-top">
                        <span class="astro-badge">⚡ Built with Astro</span>
                        <span class="no-react-badge">useState() not found</span>
                    </div>
                    <p>
                        This page is <strong>vanilla HTML, CSS, and JS</strong>,
                        with Astro doing the boring bundling work in the
                        background. No virtual DOM, no component tree to
                        reconcile, no 200 KB of framework runtime just to render
                        a table of survivor points.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Turns out the actual DOM was always right there, taking
                        calls — <a
                            class="tech-link"
                            href="https://www.codetinkerer.com/2024/01/04/forget-virtual-dom-rediscovering-vanilla-dom.html"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener"
                            >someone else already made the case for it →</a
                        >
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <footer>
            <div class="wrap">
                <div class="footer-grid">
                    <div class="footer-brand">
                        Bounty<span style="color: var(--blood-bright)"
                            >Hunter</span
                        >.challenge
                        <p>
                            A community-made Dead by Daylight challenge by Alex
                            Russo. Not affiliated with Behaviour Interactive.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="footer-links">
                        <div class="footer-col">
                            <h4>Watch</h4>
                            <a
                                href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r4qWOwr0h0g"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener">Explainer video</a
                            >
                            <a
                                href="https://www.youtube.com/@AlexRussoYT"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener">YouTube</a
                            >
                            <a
                                href="https://www.twitch.tv/aleexrusso"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener">Twitch</a
                            >
                        </div>
                        <div class="footer-col">
                            <h4>Site</h4>
                            <a
                                href="https://github.com/Nyjako"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener">Author — Nyjako</a
                            >
                            <a
                                href="https://github.com/Nyjako/dbd-bounty-hunter"
                                target="_blank"
                                rel="noopener">Repo</a
                            >
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="footer-note">
                    Built with Astro · no survivors were permanently harmed,
                    they respawn next trial.
                </div>
            </div>
        </footer>
    </body>
</html>
